      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I ran into this just today. Had a menu I was converting from a duplicate of another, changed the type of some of the menu entries to a type that did not use a subParameter. I can understand the convenience of keeping that data in case changing the type was accidental. I would propose that an \"Unused/Undefined subtype parameter(s)\" Error with an autofix that could clear unused subtypes could be used to to opt for the user to be able to fix this from validations while preserving the convenience of temporary/accidental asset editings.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
